WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:02.210
Once he settled
comfortably with hips and

00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:05.360
shoulders square and
wearing his helmet, they

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:07.370
begin taking
measurements, starting

00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:09.320
with the height of his
head, critical for

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:12.680
aerodynamics and of his
sightline over the hood,

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:14.060
critical for safety.

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:17.810
The driver sits down,
gets out, gets back in

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:20.870
several times over as
the technicians measure

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:22.280
and make adjustments.

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:25.340
When it's all done, they
run the vacuum for

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:28.400
another four hours and
then let the foam cure

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:32.160
overnight. The driver
returns for a final 2 to

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:35.120
3 hour sitting, during
which the techs trim the

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:37.910
foam as closely as
possible to the contour

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:41.700
of his body onto this
dull surface.

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:45.590
They adhere positioning
targets, reflective dots

00:00:45.590 --> 00:00:48.230
spaced four inches
apart, which create a

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:50.750
grid pattern over the
entire template.

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:54.410
The 3D laser scanner
reads these reflective

00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:58.490
dots, which a computer
translates into a 3D

00:00:58.490 --> 00:00:59.300
image.

